WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.017
Organizations use OSINT because significant security and risk information often appears outside their internal systems.

00:00:06.017 --> 00:00:09.173
Public sources may reveal exposed services, impersonation attempts,

00:00:09.173 --> 00:00:12.329
changes in business relationships, emerging threats, infrastructure dependencies,

00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:14.302
or events that affect operations.

00:00:14.302 --> 00:00:18.641
Security and threat-intelligence teams use public reporting to understand adversary behavior,

00:00:18.641 --> 00:00:20.614
vulnerabilities, campaigns, and defensive priorities.

00:00:20.614 --> 00:00:25.348
Incident responders may compare internal observations with public indicators or vendor advisories.

00:00:25.348 --> 00:00:29.293
Fraud teams and due-diligence professionals may evaluate claims, ownership, reputation,

00:00:29.293 --> 00:00:30.476
and business risk.

00:00:30.476 --> 00:00:34.421
Journalists, researchers, and risk managers use public records, reporting, imagery,

00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:37.971
and time-based evidence to verify events and explain relationships.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.733
The same source can serve different purposes,

00:00:40.733 --> 00:00:47.045
so analysts must state the question and avoid treating collection as proof of a predetermined conclusion.

00:00:47.045 --> 00:00:51.779
Public information can expose patterns that are invisible in a single record.

00:00:51.779 --> 00:00:55.724
A domain registration change, a company announcement, a code-repository update,

00:00:55.724 --> 00:01:00.458
and an official filing may become meaningful when placed on a timeline.

00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:05.191
Relationships can also be misunderstood when names, dates, or identifiers are ambiguous.

00:01:05.191 --> 00:01:06.375
Context determines significance.

00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:11.503
An internet address may be shared, reassigned, or part of a hosted service.

00:01:11.503 --> 00:01:15.448
An old profile may no longer describe a person's role.

00:01:15.448 --> 00:01:20.577
An image may be genuine but unrelated to the claimed time or location.

00:01:20.577 --> 00:01:23.338
Findings should account for these alternative explanations.

00:01:23.338 --> 00:01:26.889
Good OSINT reduces uncertainty enough to support a decision;

00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:29.256
it does not promise perfect knowledge.

00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:34.384
Analysts should explain what is known, what remains uncertain, why the finding matters,

00:01:34.384 --> 00:01:37.540
and what additional information would change the assessment.
